From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Robert McFadden <robert.mcfadden@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 20:23:34 -0500
Subject: [PATCH] Shader split: Rockstar RPF6 archives, RAGE rgxd effects and
 Double Eleven packs

Red Dead Redemption keeps its RomFS in 134 RPF6 archives with encrypted tables, and its shaders in RAGE
effects (rgxd) in shaders.rpf and in main; the language selection's two shaders are in a Double Eleven
.pkdswitch pack. The split found none of them.

dm/gfx/tools/rpf6.py reads RPF6: the tables are AES-256 ECB decrypted 16 times with a key it finds in main's
data segment (never printed or written), names by joaat hash, plain files (raw, zstd, zlib, raw deflate),
resources with RSC5 / RSC85 headers, and encrypted scripts. shader_split.py reads every archive's files in
parallel ranges, reads rgxd effects in files and in main, and reads .pkdswitch packs through their
.pkiswitch index. A control section is compared at its own length (+0x20), as 919 of the game's carry bytes
past it. 3,583 shaders, all translated; the fuzz harness has an rgxd seed. docs/reference/shaders.md: two
entries.

Upstream-Status: forwarded seedds/nxnative#2005
Reason: Red Dead Redemption's shaders are in Rockstar RPF6 archives and a Double Eleven pack, which the split could not read. Goes upstream
Issue: LNPANDY/NX2Apple#999

